  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (1633.33€) and then comparing each lottery based on how often their outcomes exceed this value. This involves evaluating which outcomes are above 1633.33€ (2500€ and 2400€ both are) and then comparing the probabilities of those favorable outcomes (33% vs 34%). However, the individual in the verbal report does not reference any such threshold or comparison to an average outcome. Instead, they focus directly on the trade-off between the change in probability and the change in payoff. Their reasoning is comparative between the two lotteries in terms of marginal changes, not in terms of deviations from an aspiration level. There is no evidence that the individual calculated or used the mean of the outcomes, nor that they assessed whether outcomes were above or below such a value. The justification is based on intuitive cost-benefit reasoning rather than aspiration-level logic. Therefore, the cognitive process described does not align with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
