  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities), then comparing the probability of outcomes above this level. The aspiration level (-3000) is not mentioned or implied in the report. The individual does not reference any calculation involving all outcomes or a reference point derived from them. Instead, they focus exclusively on the probability of incurring no loss (i.e., 0 Euros), which is a common heuristic in loss-averse decision-making. While both Lottery A and B have the same 75% probability of outcomes above the aspiration level (including -2000 and 0), the individual only emphasizes the 75% chance of zero loss, which applies only to Lottery A. This suggests they are not considering -2000 as a 'positive difference' relative to a reference point, but rather as a loss. Therefore, the information considered by the individual (presence/absence of loss, probability of zero loss) differs from the information required by the decision reason (deviations from aspiration level). The justification based on avoiding losses rather than exceeding an aspiration level further indicates a different decision rule. There is no evidence the individual computed or used the aspiration level or evaluated outcomes based on their deviation from it.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

